  "_comment": "Live-path loudness baseline (goal item 6): all 159 genres, measured on the tree that has feat/genre-instrument-curation merged (v1.16.17 + curated timbres) and BEFORE any per-genre mix or loudness trim. Producer: scripts/measure_live_loudness.mjs --all, which taps the app's realtime engine at AudioContext.destination over 1.8s of playback (post-limiter) in a real Chromium. METRIC WARNING: this is windowed broadband RMS, which averages in the silence between hits. It is NOT the same metric as the gated ITU-R BS.1770-4 integrated loudness (LUFS) used by the offline per-genre report (scripts/loudness.baseline.json), and the two disagree systematically on sparse material: ambient reads -24.7 dBFS RMS but only about -21.7 LUFS, because the gate discards the silence that dominates its RMS. Primary acceptance therefore uses the LUFS report; this file is the independent cross-check on a different metric and a different signal path (live engine vs offline render).",
